{
  "version": "Notebook/1.0",
  "items": [
    {
      "type": 1,
      "content": {
        "json": "## Coverage\nThis workbook has been created to provide a consolidated view of coverage for Defender for Cloud plans and offerings across all selected subscriptions and multi-cloud connectors.\n\n<svg viewBox=\"0 0 19 19\" width=\"20\" class=\"fxt-escapeShadow\" role=\"presentation\" focusable=\"false\" xmlns:svg=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><g><path fill=\"#1b93eb\" d=\"M16.82 8.886c0 4.81-5.752 8.574-7.006 9.411a.477.477 0 01-.523 0C8.036 17.565 2.18 13.7 2.18 8.886V3.135a.451.451 0 01.42-.419C7.2 2.612 6.154.625 9.5.625s2.3 1.987 6.8 2.091a.479.479 0 01.523.419z\"></path><path fill=\"url(#0024423711759027356)\" d=\"M16.192 8.99c0 4.392-5.333 7.947-6.483 8.575a.319.319 0 01-.418 0c-1.15-.732-6.483-4.183-6.483-8.575V3.762a.575.575 0 01.313-.523C7.2 3.135 6.258 1.357 9.4 1.357s2.2 1.882 6.274 1.882a.45.45 0 01.419.418z\"></path><path d=\"M9.219 5.378a.313.313 0 01.562 0l.875 1.772a.314.314 0 00.236.172l1.957.284a.314.314 0 01.174.535l-1.416 1.38a.312.312 0 00-.09.278l.334 1.949a.313.313 0 01-.455.33l-1.75-.92a.314.314 0 00-.292 0l-1.75.92a.313.313 0 01-.455-.33L7.483 9.8a.312.312 0 00-.09-.278L5.977 8.141a.314.314 0 01.174-.535l1.957-.284a.314.314 0 00.236-.172z\" class=\"msportalfx-svg-c01\"></path></g></svg>&nbsp;<span style=\"font-family: Open Sans; font-weight: 620; font-size: 14px;font-style: bold;margin:-10px 0px 0px 0px;position: relative;top:-3px;left:-4px;\"> Please take the time to answer a quick survey. To submit your feedback,\n</span>[<span style=\"font-family: Open Sans; font-weight: 620; font-size: 14px;font-style: bold;margin:-10px 0px 0px 0px;position: relative;top:-3px;left:-4px;\"> click here. </span>](https://aka.ms/mdfcsurveycoverageworkbook)"
      },
      "name": "Defender for Cloud Coverage"
    },
    {
      "type": 9,
      "content": {
        "version": "KqlParameterItem/1.0",
        "parameters": [
          {
            "id": "7a8be0a4-2557-43c9-afb5-9e3c9fdc11f7",
            "version": "KqlParameterItem/1.0",
            "name": "Subscriptions",
            "type": 6,
            "isRequired": true,
            "multiSelect": true,
            "quote": "'",
            "delimiter": ",",
            "value": [
              "value::all"
            ],
            "typeSettings": {
              "additionalResourceOptions": [
                "value::all"
              ],
              "includeAll": true,
              "showDefault": false
            }
          },
          {
            "id": "d4e04df2-4d8b-4127-b769-de821c7895db",
            "version": "KqlParameterItem/1.0",
            "name": "info",
            "label": "Additional information",
            "type": 10,
            "isRequired": true,
            "value": "Off",
            "typeSettings": {
              "additionalResourceOptions": []
            },
            "jsonData": "[\n { \"value\": \"On\", \"label\": \"On\"},\n { \"value\": \"Off\", \"label\": \"Off\"}\n]",
            "timeContext": {
              "durationMs": 86400000
            }
          },
          {
            "id": "f22a92ae-4573-499f-8921-8857be250f14",
            "version": "KqlParameterItem/1.0",
            "name": "relativeCoverage",
            "label": "Relative coverage",
            "type": 10,
            "isRequired": true,
            "typeSettings": {
              "additionalResourceOptions": []
            },
            "jsonData": "[\n { \"value\": \"Yes\", \"label\": \"Yes\"},\n { \"value\": \"No\", \"label\": \"No\"}\n]",
            "timeContext": {
              "durationMs": 86400000
            },
            "value": "Yes"
          },
          {
            "id": "49faad8a-8c99-4343-b11b-be188eb082a6",
            "version": "KqlParameterItem/1.0",
            "name": "absoluteCoverage",
            "type": 10,
            "isRequired": true,
            "typeSettings": {
              "additionalResourceOptions": []
            },
            "jsonData": "[\n { \"value\": \"Yes\", \"label\": \"Yes\"},\n { \"value\": \"No\", \"label\": \"No\"}\n]",
            "timeContext": {
              "durationMs": 86400000
            },
            "value": "Yes",
            "label": "Absolute coverage"
          },
          {
            "id": "d5c581af-3a66-401b-8862-dc2950449389",
            "version": "KqlParameterItem/1.0",
            "name": "detailedCoverage",
            "label": "Detailed coverage",
            "type": 10,
            "isRequired": true,
            "typeSettings": {
              "additionalResourceOptions": []
            },
            "jsonData": "[\n { \"value\": \"Yes\", \"label\": \"Yes\"},\n { \"value\": \"No\", \"label\": \"No\"}\n]",
            "timeContext": {
              "durationMs": 86400000
            },
            "value": "Yes"
          }
        ],
        "style": "above",
        "queryType": 0,
        "resourceType": "microsoft.operationalinsights/workspaces"
      },
      "name": "info"
    },
    {
      "type": 1,
      "content": {
        "json": "Use the different filter options above to show relative, absolute, and detailed coverage for your environment.\n\n- **Relative coverage** shows the percentage of subscriptions/connectors that have a particular Defender for Cloud plan enabled.\n- **Absolute coverage** shows each plan's status per subscription.\n- The **detailed coverage** section has been added to show additional settings that can/need to be enabled on relevant plans in order to get each plan's full value.\n\n**Azure Defender CSPM components:** After Subscription Name, the component columns appear left to right in the same order as the top-to-bottom Defender CSPM settings list:\n\n1. Agentless scanning for machines\n2. Kubernetes API access\n3. Registry access\n4. Sensitive data discovery\n5. Cloud Infrastructure and Entitlements Management (CIEM)\n6. API Security Posture Management\n7. Serverless protection\n8. Serverless containers\n\n**Enabled** and **Disabled** reflect the reported component setting. **Not reported** means the setting is missing, empty, or unrecognized in Azure Resource Graph; it must not be interpreted as disabled. These are configuration states, not confirmation of successful scanning or resource-level protection. Serverless containers require Registry access for full coverage. See [Defender CSPM components](https://learn.microsoft.com/azure/defender-for-cloud/tutorial-enable-cspm-plan#enable-the-components-of-the-defender-cspm-plan).\n\nFor Defender for AI Services, detailed coverage reports suspicious prompt evidence and AI Model Security (Preview) component settings. Not reported means a component setting was absent or unrecognized, not necessarily disabled. Component configuration does not establish that models were scanned.\n\n**Portal-aligned detailed coverage:** AWS and GCP columns follow the sampled Defender for Cloud settings order; existing data-aware database posture fields remain after the portal settings. In the updated Azure Servers and Containers and AWS/GCP detailed views, missing or unrecognized settings are **Not reported**, not Disabled. CIEM is Not reported when no explicit enabled value is available; configuration-object presence alone does not establish its state. Some portal settings, including AWS CloudTrail ingestion, Azure Policy and agent provisioning settings, do not have a verified Resource Graph enabled field and are not reported as enabled or disabled.\n\n**Defender for Servers:** Agentless scanning and File Integrity Monitoring reflect the subscription's Servers pricing extensions. **Not included in Servers P1** does not rule out coverage from another plan. These settings do not confirm protection of individual machines.\n\n**Defender for Storage:** Detailed coverage includes subscriptions using the `DefenderForStorageV2` sub-plan; other Storage pricing options remain included in overall coverage. It reports malware-scanning state, the per-account monthly scanning cap in GB/month, and sensitive data discovery. The cap is already expressed in GB/month/account; -1 means unlimited. Missing or unrecognized values are Not reported, and storage-account overrides can differ from subscription settings.\n\nThe Activity monitoring table samples seven days of Blob and File service transactions and Blob upload ingress, then projects them to 30 days. Modeled scanning is the lesser of projected Blob uploads and the Activity model cap. The cap is a scenario input, not automatically populated from the subscription-level cap; use accounts with the same cap when comparing a capped scenario. This is a model, not measured malware scans, and does not prove that scanning is enabled or that all uploads are scanned. Multiple scans, unscannable blobs, and missing metrics can make actual scanned volume differ. Missing metrics leave affected modeled values blank, not zero; accounts with no metric rows may be omitted. [Storage plan configuration](https://learn.microsoft.com/azure/defender-for-cloud/defender-for-storage-powershell-enablement).\n\n**Defender for APIs:** Absolute coverage shows the subscription-level status and reported plan. A missing or unrecognized status is Not reported; an enabled plan with no reported sub-plan is shown as plan not reported. An enabled subscription plan does not confirm that individual APIs are onboarded or protected.\n\n**JFrog Artifactory:** Plan states are based on reported connector offerings. Missing, empty, or unrecognized offerings are Not reported; a plan absent from a recognized offering list is Disabled. Relative percentages exclude unreported plans, and the table counts connectors with unreported plans. The detailed table reports the configured scan interval and the Defender CSPM image assessment setting when supplied. This CSPM setting does not establish whether the Containers plan is scanning. Plan and component configuration does not establish connection health, full monitoring coverage, or successful scans. See [JFrog onboarding](https://learn.microsoft.com/azure/defender-for-cloud/agentless-vulnerability-assessment-jfrog-artifactory).\n\n**GCP CSPM:** Cloud Logging ingestion is reported from the explicit `ciemDiscovery.enableAuditLogIngestion` setting when available, separately from its provisioning method and any Pub/Sub subscription names reported in `ciem.gcpAuditLogIngestion.resourceSets`. The method or subscription name does not prove ingestion is enabled or working, and names are not inferred from resource prefixes. Missing or unrecognized values are Not reported. A connector with multiple reported Pub/Sub subscriptions appears once per resource set (up to 2,000); missing or empty resource sets retain one row. The schema documents these properties, but their availability in Resource Graph and final portal rendering are not verified. See [GCP Cloud Logging ingestion](https://learn.microsoft.com/azure/defender-for-cloud/logging-ingestion) and the [security connector schema](https://learn.microsoft.com/azure/templates/microsoft.security/2026-08-01-preview/securityconnectors).\n\n**AWS CSPM:** Foundational CSPM is based on the reported `CspmMonitorAws` offering. When that offering is absent, its status is Not reported and excluded from its relative coverage percentage; the relative table counts connectors with unreported Foundational CSPM. The AWS CloudTrail ingestion column reports the provisioning method when supplied, not an enabled state; it does not establish whether CloudTrail ingestion is enabled or working. Missing or unrecognized methods are Not reported. Conflicting legacy and current serverless protection values are Not reported. See [CloudTrail ingestion](https://learn.microsoft.com/azure/defender-for-cloud/integrate-cloud-trail).\n\n\n**AWS Databases:** Detailed coverage reports the documented `rds.enabled` (Open-source relational databases), `arcAutoProvisioning.enabled` (Azure Arc agent), and `databasesDspm.enabled` settings. The published `DefenderForDatabasesAws` schema does not expose a separate SQL Servers on machines switch or its portal 1/3 readiness score; those values are not inferred from Databases plan presence or Arc auto-provisioning. See the [security connector schema](https://learn.microsoft.com/azure/templates/microsoft.security/2026-08-01-preview/securityconnectors).\n\n**GCP Databases:** Detailed coverage reports **Azure Arc agent** from the connector's `DefenderForDatabasesGcp.arcAutoProvisioning.enabled` setting and **SQL servers on machines** from the Azure subscription's `SqlServerVirtualMachines` pricing resource. The SQL plan status is subscription-scoped and repeats for GCP connectors in that subscription; it is not a per-project setting. The separate **Azure Monitoring Agent for SQL server on machines** provisioning toggle is not exposed by the documented GCP connector schema and has no verified Resource Graph source in this workbook, so it is not shown as a portal-only check. These settings do not confirm SQL protection or agent installation. See [GCP plan configuration](https://learn.microsoft.com/azure/defender-for-cloud/configure-google-plans), [SQL servers on machines](https://learn.microsoft.com/azure/defender-for-cloud/defender-for-sql-usage), and the [security connector schema](https://learn.microsoft.com/azure/templates/microsoft.security/2026-08-01-preview/securityconnectors).\n\n**AWS Containers:** Details show Agentless scanning, Agentless threat protection, the audit-log retention period in days, Defender sensor auto-provisioning, Azure Policy extension auto-provisioning, Kubernetes API access, and Registry access. The retention value comes from the reported `kubeAuditRetentionTime`; missing or invalid values are **Not reported**. Configuration does not establish that agents, policies, or runtime protections are active on individual clusters.\n\n**AWS Servers:** Details show Agentless scanning, Azure Arc agent auto-provisioning, and the two reported additional Arc extensions: Defender for Endpoint and Vulnerability assessment. The extension summary shows the enabled count out of two; missing or unrecognized values remain Not reported and are not counted as disabled. These connector settings do not confirm extension installation on individual machines.\n\n**GCP Servers:** Details show Agentless scanning, Azure Arc agent, and the two reported additional extensions for Arc connected machines: Defender for Endpoint and Vulnerability assessment. The summary counts explicitly enabled extensions; missing or unrecognized values remain Not reported and are not counted as disabled. These connector settings do not confirm extension installation on individual machines."
      },
      "conditionalVisibility": {
        "parameterName": "info",
        "comparison": "isEqualTo",
        "value": "On"
      },
      "name": "infoText"
    },
    {
      "type": 1,
      "content": {
        "json": "## Release notes\n\n|Version|Description|Date|\n|---|---|---|\n| v1.0 | initial release, public availability of Defender for Cloud Coverage Workbook | January 20, 2022 |\n| v1.1 | adding navigation menu and coverage for AWS connectors | February 21, 2022 |\n| v1.2 | Updating AWS query and adding coverage for GCP connectors after API update | March 23, 2022|\n| v1.3 | adding Defender for Servers P1/P2 | April 7, 2022 |\n| v1.4 | adding relative coverage | April 14, 2022 |\n| v1.5 | adding coverage for Defender for Databases on multicloud connectors | June 27, 2022|\n| v1.6 | adding coverage for Defender CSPM | October 12, 2022 |\n| v1.7 | adding information about Defender for Storage pricing tier | February 28, 2023 |\n| v1.8 | updating queries for business model changes in Defender for Resource Manager, DNS, Key Vault | July 31, 2023|\n| v1.9 | adding detailed coverage for relevant plans' extensions | September 08, 2023|\n| v1.10 | adding detailed coverage for multicloud connectors | November 08, 2023|\n| v1.11 | adding Azure CSPM API posture, Serverless protection, and Serverless containers settings; distinguishing unreported settings from disabled components | October 28, 2026|\n| v1.12 | adding Defender for AI Services plan and detailed component coverage | November 23, 2026 |\n| v1.13 | aligning Azure, AWS and GCP detailed coverage with portal settings; adding supported container, serverless and database components; updating Defender for Storage labels | November 24, 2026 |\n| v1.14 | adding Defender for Storage plan, monthly scanning cap, and non-cost activity monitoring | November 24, 2026 |\n| v1.15 | adding detailed Defender for APIs status and configured plan | November 24, 2026 |\n| v1.16 | adding APIs to Azure absolute coverage and consolidating Azure database coverage with resource-type details | November 24, 2026 |\n| v1.17 | showing reported plan variants in Azure absolute coverage and removing duplicate plan columns from details | November 24, 2026 |\n| v1.18 | adding subscription and asset-level SQL servers on machines diagnostics | November 24, 2026 |\n| v1.19 | adding host-level Arc SQL extension overview with architecture-aware status reporting | November 24, 2026 |\n| v1.20 | clarifying database plan coverage count as Enabled (x/x Plans) | November 24, 2026 |\n| v1.21 | correcting SQL machine subscription filtering and query limits; removing unreported Azure Containers placeholder columns | November 24, 2026 |\n| v1.22 | adding JFrog Artifactory connector plan coverage and reported configuration details | November 24, 2026 |\n| v1.23 | aligning AWS CSPM settings and adding Foundational CSPM and reported CloudTrail provisioning | November 24, 2026 |\n| v1.24 | adding AWS Servers Arc extension summary and detailed settings | November 24, 2026 |\n| v1.25 | documenting AWS Databases settings and SQL Servers on machines schema limitations | November 24, 2026 |\n| v1.26 | adding the AWS Containers audit-log retention period to detailed coverage | November 24, 2026 |\n| v1.27 | adding reported GCP Cloud Logging ingestion settings to Defender CSPM details | November 24, 2026 |\n| v1.28 | aligning GCP Servers details with the portal's Arc extension summary | November 24, 2026 |\n| v1.29 | adding subscription-level SQL servers on machines status to GCP Databases details and documenting the unreported AMA provisioning toggle | November 24, 2026 |"
      },
      "conditionalVisibility": {
        "parameterName": "info",
        "comparison": "isEqualTo",
        "value": "On"
      },
      "name": "releaseNotes"
    },
    {
      "type": 11,
      "content": {
